IMPORT prelude

-- Montana Code Annotated 2025, Title 39, chapter 51 (unemployment insurance), parts 2, 21, 22 and 23 -- the
-- seat-neutral core: the base period (39-51-201(2)), qualifying wages (39-51-2105), the weekly benefit amount and its
-- minimum and maximum (39-51-2201), the maximum benefit amount (39-51-2204), total unemployment and the week's payment
-- (39-51-2101, 39-51-2104(2), 39-51-2202, 39-51-2203), the weekly eligibility conditions (39-51-2104(1)), the
-- disqualifications for leaving work, discharge and refusing suitable work (39-51-2302 to 39-51-2304), suitable work
-- (39-51-2304(2)-(4)), and the duties at a new claim and on double payment (39-51-2207, 39-51-2208(2), 39-51-2306(2)).
--
-- Edition: Montana Code Annotated 2025 (laws through the 2025 session), site marked "Updated August 2026", as deposited
-- at ../../registers/source-bundle/mca-39-51-part-2.txt, -part-21.txt, -part-22.txt, -part-23.txt (retrieved 2026-10-19
-- UTC). The average annual wage (39-51-2201(2)) and the contribution schedule in force (39-51-1218, not deposited) are
-- set each year and are inputs.
--
-- The federal frame (FUTA s 3304, SSA Title III, EUCA 1970) is in subjects/us/internal-revenue-code-of-1986/ and
-- subjects/us/social-security-act/ (cross-folder IMPORT is not possible; NOTES.md names the link).
--
-- The seat questions are in mt-ui-seat.l4. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Montana unemployment insurance -- core`

§§ `Arithmetic`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest cent` x MEANS (FLOOR ((x TIMES 100) PLUS 0.5)) DIVIDED BY 100

-- The sum of the two largest of four quarters.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER, c IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the two highest of` a b c d MEANS
    maximum (LIST (a PLUS b), (a PLUS c), (a PLUS d), (b PLUS c), (b PLUS d), (c PLUS d))

§§ `39-51-201(2) -- the base period, and 39-51-2105 -- qualifying wages`

-- Wages paid in each of the last 5 completed calendar quarters before the benefit year, oldest first.
DECLARE `Quarterly wages` HAS
    `quarter 1 (oldest)` IS A NUMBER
    `quarter 2`          IS A NUMBER
    `quarter 3`          IS A NUMBER
    `quarter 4`          IS A NUMBER
    `quarter 5 (most recent)` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Base period wages` HAS
    `total base period wages`        IS A NUMBER
    `high quarter wages`             IS A NUMBER
    `two highest quarters wages`     IS A NUMBER

-- 39-51-201(2)(a): "the first 4 of the last 5 completed calendar quarters".
GIVEN w IS A `Quarterly wages`
GIVETH A `Base period wages`
`the regular base period` w MEANS
    `Base period wages` WITH
        `total base period wages`    IS ((w's `quarter 1 (oldest)` PLUS w's `quarter 2`) PLUS w's `quarter 3`) PLUS w's `quarter 4`
        `high quarter wages`         IS maximum (LIST w's `quarter 1 (oldest)`, w's `quarter 2`, w's `quarter 3`, w's `quarter 4`)
        `two highest quarters wages` IS `the two highest of` (w's `quarter 1 (oldest)`) (w's `quarter 2`) (w's `quarter 3`) (w's `quarter 4`)

-- 39-51-201(2)(b): if not enough to qualify under (a), "the 4 most recently completed calendar quarters".
GIVEN w IS A `Quarterly wages`
GIVETH A `Base period wages`
`the alternative base period` w MEANS
    `Base period wages` WITH
        `total base period wages`    IS ((w's `quarter 2` PLUS w's `quarter 3`) PLUS w's `quarter 4`) PLUS w's `quarter 5 (most recent)`
        `high quarter wages`         IS maximum (LIST w's `quarter 2`, w's `quarter 3`, w's `quarter 4`, w's `quarter 5 (most recent)`)
        `two highest quarters wages` IS `the two highest of` (w's `quarter 2`) (w's `quarter 3`) (w's `quarter 4`) (w's `quarter 5 (most recent)`)

-- 39-51-2105: total base period wages "(1) not less than 1 1/2 times the wages earned in the calendar quarter in which
-- wages were the highest during the base period; however, the total wages in the base period must be equal to or
-- greater than 7% of the average annual wage described in 39-51-2201; or (2) equal to or greater than 50% of the
-- average annual wage".
GIVEN bp IS A `Base period wages`, `average annual wage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has qualifying wages` bp `average annual wage` IF
        (    bp's `total base period wages` AT LEAST (1.5 TIMES bp's `high quarter wages`)
         AND bp's `total base period wages` AT LEAST (0.07 TIMES `average annual wage`))
    OR  bp's `total base period wages` AT LEAST (0.5 TIMES `average annual wage`)

DECLARE `Which base period` IS ONE OF
    `the regular base period (the first 4 of the last 5 completed quarters)`
    `the alternative base period (the 4 most recently completed quarters)`
    `neither: the wages do not qualify`

GIVEN w IS A `Quarterly wages`, `average annual wage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Which base period`
`the base period that qualifies` w `average annual wage` MEANS
    IF `has qualifying wages` (`the regular base period` w) `average annual wage`
    THEN `the regular base period (the first 4 of the last 5 completed quarters)`
    ELSE IF `has qualifying wages` (`the alternative base period` w) `average annual wage`
         THEN `the alternative base period (the 4 most recently completed quarters)`
         ELSE `neither: the wages do not qualify`

GIVEN w IS A `Quarterly wages`, `average annual wage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Base period wages`
`the qualifying base period wages` w `average annual wage` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the base period that qualifies` w `average annual wage`
    WHEN `the regular base period (the first 4 of the last 5 completed quarters)` THEN JUST (`the regular base period` w)
    WHEN `the alternative base period (the 4 most recently completed quarters)` THEN JUST (`the alternative base period` w)
    WHEN `neither: the wages do not qualify` THEN NOTHING

§§ `39-51-2201 -- the weekly benefit amount`

-- (2): the average weekly wage is the average annual wage "divided by 52, rounded to the nearest cent".
-- (3)(a): if the contribution schedule under 39-51-1218 is Schedule II or higher, the maximum is 66.5% and the minimum
-- 19% of the average weekly wage; (3)(b): under Schedule I, 67.5% and 20%. The text does not round them (NOTES.md
-- finding 3).
GIVEN `average annual wage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the average weekly wage` `average annual wage` MEANS `rounded to the nearest cent` (`average annual wage` DIVIDED BY 52)

GIVEN `average annual wage` IS A NUMBER, `schedule I is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum weekly benefit amount` `average annual wage` `schedule I is in force` MEANS
    IF `schedule I is in force`
    THEN 0.675 TIMES `the average weekly wage` `average annual wage`
    ELSE 0.665 TIMES `the average weekly wage` `average annual wage`

GIVEN `average annual wage` IS A NUMBER, `schedule I is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum weekly benefit amount` `average annual wage` `schedule I is in force` MEANS
    IF `schedule I is in force`
    THEN 0.2 TIMES `the average weekly wage` `average annual wage`
    ELSE 0.19 TIMES `the average weekly wage` `average annual wage`

-- (1): "an amount equal to 1% of the total base period wages or equal to 1.9% of the total wages paid in the 2
-- calendar quarters in which wages were the highest during the base period", rounded down to the dollar, and not less
-- than the minimum or more than the maximum. The text does not say which of the two; this encoding takes the greater
-- (NOTES.md finding 2).
GIVEN bp IS A `Base period wages`, `average annual wage` IS A NUMBER, `schedule I is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekly benefit amount` bp `average annual wage` `schedule I is in force` MEANS
    min (`the maximum weekly benefit amount` `average annual wage` `schedule I is in force`)
        (max (`the minimum weekly benefit amount` `average annual wage` `schedule I is in force`) rounded)
    WHERE
        rounded MEANS FLOOR (max (0.01 TIMES bp's `total base period wages`) (0.019 TIMES bp's `two highest quarters wages`))

§§ `39-51-2204 -- the maximum benefit amount`

-- Full weeks of benefits by the ratio of total base period earnings to the high quarter.
GIVEN ratio IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the full weeks of benefits for the ratio` ratio MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF ratio LESS THAN 1.25 THEN 8
        IF ratio LESS THAN 1.5 THEN 10
        IF ratio LESS THAN 1.75 THEN 12
        IF ratio LESS THAN 2 THEN 14
        IF ratio LESS THAN 2.25 THEN 16
        IF ratio LESS THAN 2.5 THEN 18
        IF ratio LESS THAN 2.75 THEN 20
        IF ratio LESS THAN 3 THEN 22
        OTHERWISE 24

GIVEN bp IS A `Base period wages`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the full weeks of benefits` bp MEANS
    IF bp's `high quarter wages` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `the full weeks of benefits for the ratio` (bp's `total base period wages` DIVIDED BY bp's `high quarter wages`)
    ELSE 0

§§ `39-51-2101, 39-51-2104, 39-51-2202, 39-51-2203 -- one week`

DECLARE `The week` HAS
    `hours worked in the week`                               IS A NUMBER
    `wages earned in the week`                               IS A NUMBER
    `worked fewer hours than usual because of a lack of work` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days or part-days unavailable for work in the week`     IS A NUMBER
    -- 39-51-2203(1), only where (a), (b) apply and (2) does not
    `pension reasonably attributable to the week that must be deducted` IS A NUMBER
    -- 39-51-2104(1)
    `filed the claim and continued claims as the rules require`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `able to work, available for work and seeking work`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `has served the 1-week waiting period`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered for work with the local job service, or excused`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- 39-51-2101: totally unemployed in a week in which the individual "(a) did not perform any work in employment and did
-- not earn any wages", or "(b) (i) due to a lack of work, worked fewer than the hours that are typically worked ... and
-- (ii) earned wages ... less than two times the individual's weekly benefit amount"; (2) never in a week of 40 hours.
GIVEN wk IS A `The week`, wba IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is totally unemployed in the week` wk wba IF
        wk's `hours worked in the week` LESS THAN 40
    AND (    (    wk's `hours worked in the week` EQUALS 0
              AND wk's `wages earned in the week` EQUALS 0)
         OR  (    wk's `worked fewer hours than usual because of a lack of work`
              AND wk's `wages earned in the week` LESS THAN (2 TIMES wba)))

-- 39-51-2104(1)(a)-(d), as found by the department; (2)(b): unavailable 3 days or more, no benefits for the week.
GIVEN wk IS A `The week`, wba IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is eligible for the week` wk wba IF
        `is totally unemployed in the week` wk wba
    AND wk's `filed the claim and continued claims as the rules require`
    AND wk's `able to work, available for work and seeking work`
    AND wk's `has served the 1-week waiting period`
    AND wk's `registered for work with the local job service, or excused`
    AND wk's `days or part-days unavailable for work in the week` LESS THAN 3

-- 39-51-2104(2)(a): unavailable fewer than 3 days, "reduced by one-fifth of that amount for each day or part of a day".
-- 39-51-2202: partial payment is "the claimant's weekly benefit amount less 50% of wages for employment earned in excess
-- of one-fourth of the claimant's weekly benefit amount", each rounded down to the dollar.
-- 39-51-2203: reduced "(but not below zero)" by a pension attributable to the week.
-- The text does not order the three reductions; this encoding applies the availability fifths and the earnings to the
-- weekly benefit amount and then the pension (NOTES.md finding 5).
GIVEN wk IS A `The week`, wba IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the payment for the week` wk wba MEANS
    IF `is eligible for the week` wk wba
    THEN max 0 ((afterAvailability MINUS earningsDeduction) MINUS wk's `pension reasonably attributable to the week that must be deducted`)
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        afterAvailability MEANS wba MINUS ((wba DIVIDED BY 5) TIMES (CEILING (wk's `days or part-days unavailable for work in the week`)))
        earningsDeduction MEANS 0.5 TIMES (max 0 ((FLOOR (wk's `wages earned in the week`)) MINUS (FLOOR (wba DIVIDED BY 4))))

§§ `39-51-2302 to 39-51-2304 -- disqualifications`

-- How the claimant's last job ended, as the department determines it. "Misconduct" and "gross misconduct" are defined in
-- 39-51-201(19) and (13); the finding is the department's, so it is an input.
DECLARE `How the job ended` IS ONE OF
    `laid off for lack of work`
    `I quit with good cause attributable to my employment`
    `I quit without good cause attributable to my employment`
    `discharged, but not for misconduct`
    `discharged for misconduct`
    `discharged for gross misconduct, as the department determines`
    `discharged for failing or refusing an employer drug test under a written policy`

DECLARE `Disqualification` IS ONE OF
    `not disqualified`
    `disqualified until I earn, after the week of the act, wages of at least` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `disqualified for 52 weeks`
    `disqualified, with no end stated in the text`

-- 39-51-2302(2): a quit is not disqualifying for (a) illness or injury on medical advice with an offer to return on
-- recovery, (b) leaving temporary work to return to the regular employer, (c) a military order of under 180 days
-- after which the job had ended, (d) a spouse's mandatory military transfer. (3): to requalify, services paid at least
-- six times the weekly benefit amount, unless in regular attendance at an accredited Montana educational institution for
-- at least 3 consecutive months from the act.
-- 39-51-2303(1): misconduct, until services paid at least eight times the weekly benefit amount; (2) gross misconduct,
-- 52 weeks; (3) a failed or refused drug test (not a marijuana test of a registered cardholder): no period is stated.
GIVEN `how the job ended` IS A `How the job ended`
      `a 39-51-2302(2) exception applies to my quit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I attended an accredited Montana school for 3 consecutive months since the act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the drug test was for marijuana and I am a registered cardholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      wba IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Disqualification`
`the disqualification for the separation` `how the job ended` `a 39-51-2302(2) exception applies to my quit` `I attended an accredited Montana school for 3 consecutive months since the act` `the drug test was for marijuana and I am a registered cardholder` wba MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the job ended`
    WHEN `I quit without good cause attributable to my employment` THEN
        IF     `a 39-51-2302(2) exception applies to my quit`
            OR `I attended an accredited Montana school for 3 consecutive months since the act`
        THEN `not disqualified`
        ELSE `disqualified until I earn, after the week of the act, wages of at least` (6 TIMES wba)
    WHEN `discharged for misconduct` THEN `disqualified until I earn, after the week of the act, wages of at least` (8 TIMES wba)
    WHEN `discharged for gross misconduct, as the department determines` THEN `disqualified for 52 weeks`
    WHEN `discharged for failing or refusing an employer drug test under a written policy` THEN
        IF `the drug test was for marijuana and I am a registered cardholder`
        THEN `not disqualified`
        ELSE `disqualified, with no end stated in the text`
    OTHERWISE `not disqualified`

-- 39-51-2304(3): work is never suitable, and benefits may not be denied for refusing it, if (a) the vacancy is due
-- directly to a strike, lockout or other labor dispute, (b) wages, hours or conditions are substantially less favorable
-- than those prevailing for similar work locally, or (c) the job requires joining a company union or not joining a bona
-- fide labor organization. (4): after 13 weeks of unemployment, suitable work is work meeting the criteria that offers
-- 75% of earnings in previous insured work in the customary occupation, but never below the federal minimum wage.
-- (2): otherwise the department weighs risk, fitness, experience, length of unemployment and distance (an input).
DECLARE `Job offer` HAS
    `the vacancy is due directly to a strike, lockout or other labor dispute`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `pay, hours or conditions are substantially less favorable than prevailing locally` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the job requires joining a company union or not joining a bona fide union`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the department finds it suitable on the 39-51-2304(2) factors`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `weeks of unemployment so far`                                                       IS A NUMBER
    `offered pay as a fraction of my previous insured earnings in my customary occupation` IS A NUMBER
    `the offered pay is below the federal minimum wage`                                  IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN o IS A `Job offer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is suitable work` o IF
        (NOT o's `the vacancy is due directly to a strike, lockout or other labor dispute`)
    AND (NOT o's `pay, hours or conditions are substantially less favorable than prevailing locally`)
    AND (NOT o's `the job requires joining a company union or not joining a bona fide union`)
    AND (NOT o's `the offered pay is below the federal minimum wage`)
    AND (    o's `the department finds it suitable on the 39-51-2304(2) factors`
         OR  (    o's `weeks of unemployment so far` GREATER THAN 13
              AND o's `offered pay as a fraction of my previous insured earnings in my customary occupation` AT LEAST 0.75))

-- 39-51-2304(1)(b): refusing suitable work without good cause disqualifies "for the week in which the failure occurs
-- and until" services paid at least six times the weekly benefit amount, "with a reduction in the individual's maximum
-- benefit amount equal to six times the weekly benefit amount". The department's "as determined" reading of the
-- 13-week clause is not second-guessed: the department finding is one input.

DECLARE `Refusal outcome` IS ONE OF
    `not disqualified: the work offered is not suitable work`
    `not disqualified: I had good cause`
    `disqualified for the week and until I earn wages of at least this, and my maximum benefit amount is cut by the same` HAS `six times my weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN o IS A `Job offer`, `I had good cause` IS A BOOLEAN, wba IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Refusal outcome`
`the outcome of refusing the offer` o `I had good cause` wba MEANS
    IF (NOT (`is suitable work` o))
    THEN `not disqualified: the work offered is not suitable work`
    ELSE IF `I had good cause`
         THEN `not disqualified: I had good cause`
         ELSE `disqualified for the week and until I earn wages of at least this, and my maximum benefit amount is cut by the same` (6 TIMES wba)

§§ `Duties at a new claim, and on double payment`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the claimant`
    `the department of labor and industry`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `disclose whether I owe an uncollected food stamp overissuance`
    `advise that benefits are federally taxable, that estimated tax rules exist, and that federal withholding may be elected or changed`
    `elect federal income tax withholding from benefits`
    `repay the unemployment benefits for the week`

-- 39-51-2208(2): "An individual filing a new claim for unemployment benefits shall disclose at the time of filing the
-- claim whether or not the individual owes for an uncollected overissuance of food stamp benefits".
-- 39-51-2207(1): "The department shall advise an individual at the time the individual files a new claim" that
-- benefits are subject to federal income tax, of the estimated tax requirements, and that the individual "may elect"
-- withholding and change it. "At the time" of filing is day 0 of the claim.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duties when I file a new claim` MEANS
        (PARTY `the claimant`
         MUST  `disclose whether I owe an uncollected food stamp overissuance`
         WITHIN 0
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "the claimant did not disclose at the time of the new claim whether a food stamp overissuance is owed (39-51-2208(2))")
    RAND
        (PARTY `the department of labor and industry`
         MUST  `advise that benefits are federally taxable, that estimated tax rules exist, and that federal withholding may be elected or changed`
         WITHIN 0
         HENCE (PARTY `the claimant` MAY `elect federal income tax withholding from benefits`)
         LEST  BREACH BY `the department of labor and industry` BECAUSE "the department did not advise the claimant of the tax status of benefits and the withholding election when the new claim was filed (39-51-2207(1))")

-- 39-51-2306(2): if the individual later receives workers' compensation, or other unemployment benefits, for a week
-- already paid, "the individual shall repay the unemployment benefits, and the department may collect" them under
-- 39-51-3206 (not deposited). No time for repayment is stated, so the rule has no WITHIN.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to repay a doubly paid week` MEANS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    MUST  `repay the unemployment benefits for the week`
    HENCE FULFILLED

GIVEN `received workers' compensation or other unemployment benefits for an already paid week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must repay the week` `received workers' compensation or other unemployment benefits for an already paid week` IF
    `received workers' compensation or other unemployment benefits for an already paid week`
